{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/9feasa","slide":1,"text":"[Sources]\n- User-provided GaitParity Presentation.pdf, slides 7–8.\n\nPresenter notes:\n- J is the positive area under the forward-force curve during stance; braking is excluded.\n- The sign identifies the stronger side and the absolute value gives the size of the asymmetry.\n- All three mirror operations must happen together; otherwise the geometry, joint names, and visibility pattern become inconsistent."}